                    {
                        "name":  "places/ChIJXfCvReOrQjQRs3K2Lo84HaI/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tndFRWQlRhR3RmT1RjNE5IRjNRbTlLT0hkSVdHYxAB",
                        "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "6 months ago",
                        "rating":  1,
                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "December 5th Update: I ate the beef noodles I took out yesterday today, only to find there was only half a bowl. This restaurant not only threw away a customer\u0027s food without apologizing but also only gave the customer half back. They showed no sincerity and I will not return. This is for other potential customers\u0027 reference.\n\nThe food was good, but the staff training needs improvement.\n\nService: Today I ate alone. The staff had already seated me halfway through when a foreigner approached, and they panicked, telling me I should wait at the counter while they finished. The beef noodles were 420 NTD a bowl, quite expensive, but I only got about half the value. I wanted to take the other half home, but the staff threw it into the waste bin. A waiter came out to tell me the food had been thrown away, so what? My beef noodles? Finally, perhaps noticing my upset expression, they went back to negotiate with the kitchen to give me a replacement bowl. The experience was very poor. Please improve staff training. The price is higher than Din Tai Fung, but the service is less than half as good.\n\nFood: I ordered the braised beef noodles. The noodles were thick and chewy, somewhat like knife-cut noodles. There were four pieces of beef, one of which was tendon. The beef was stewed until tender and melted in my mouth, which was commendable. The broth was decent, typical of good braised beef noodles. The other side dishes were ordinary, even a bit cheap, including tomato and tofu skin, dried tofu strips (which tasted like non-spicy konjac), and pickled mustard greens. The tea jelly seemed to be made from powder that you could buy at PX Mart, and the fruit was neither sweet nor flavorful—not good at all. I suggest focusing on beef noodles, lowering the price, or improving the quality of the other side dishes.",
                                     "languageCode":  "en-US"
                                 },
                        "originalText":  {
                                             "text":  "12/5更新\n今天拿了昨天外帶的牛肉麵吃，打開發現只有半碗。貴餐廳把客人的餐點倒掉不僅沒有致歉還只補一半給客人，毫無誠意，不會再訪，提供其他欲到訪的顧客參考。\n\n餐點好吃但服務人員的訓練要加油。\n服務部分：今天我獨自去用餐，店員都帶位到一半了結果外國人來搭話就亂了陣腳，還叫我應該在櫃檯等他先處理完^_^\n牛肉麵420一碗價格頗貴，但大概只吃到一半的價值，另一半吃不完想打包卻被員工倒進廚餘桶。服務生跑出來告知餐點被倒掉，所以呢？我的牛肉麵？最後不知道是不是看我臉色不對又進去跟後廚協商補一碗給我，觀感很差。請加強員工訓練，價格比鼎泰豐高服務沒人家一半好。\n\n餐點部分：\n我點的是紅燒牛肉麵，麵體有點像刀削麵是粗粗有嚼勁的口感。牛肉四塊其中一塊是牛筋，牛肉燉到軟爛入口即化，值得嘉許。湯頭中規中矩，是好吃的紅燒牛肉麵的味道。其他小菜很普通甚至有點廉價，有蕃茄百頁豆腐、豆乾絲（吃起來是不辣的魔芋爽味）、醃結頭菜。茶凍感覺是全聯買得到的粉泡出來的，水果不甜也沒味道，不好吃。建議專精在牛肉麵，降低定價，或是提升其他附餐品質。",
                                             "languageCode":  "zh-Hant"
                                         },
